  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 247 PM EDT Tue Sep 15 2026\n\nBy the end of the week the warm front will sag south as a cold front \nand stall near the Ohio River once again, This will bring an \nincreased chance of showers and storms (10-30 percent) mainly across \nsouthern IN and east of I-65. As of now activity looks relatively \nscattered to isolated with low QPF. This will bring slightly cooler \ntemperatures with highs in the low/mid 90s and upper 80s across the \nBluegrass. Heat advisory may need to remain in place for locations \nto the west and south for the end of the week. \n\nThe weekend looks to be split with temperatures still remaining \nunseasonably warm on Saturday as the aforementioned front lifts back \nnorth as a warm front allowing for high to get back to around the \nmid 90s and mostly dry but a weak shortwave trough working over the \ntop of the retrograding upper ridge will push a stronger cold front \nthrough by the end of the weekend and into early next week. We will \nsee an increased chance of showers and storms with this system and \ncooler temperatures into the 80s by the start of next week.",
